  "macroTheme": "Warsh's first FOMC at 18:00 GMT today -- hold 97% priced, dot plot and easing bias removal are the battleground. RBA paused unanimously Jun 16 at 4.35% after 3 consecutive hikes -- AUD soft. US30 at new ATH 52,190 while NAS100 printed a distribution candle below broken support 30,001. Gold pre-FOMC short-covering bounce exhausted at 4,369. UK CPI May Thursday is the next post-FOMC catalyst.",
  "macroOverview": "Pre-FOMC positioning bifurcated the tape. US30 printed a new all-time high at 52,190 Tuesday (value/industrial holding) while NAS100 reversed sharply -1.89% from 30,560 to 29,968 with a textbook distribution candle -- broken support 30,001 confirmed as resistance. RBA voted unanimously to hold at 4.35% on June 16, first pause after three consecutive 25bp hikes; AUD softened to 0.7062. Gold bounced +7.7% from 4,031 low on short-covering to 4,348, stalling at 4,369 intraday high. Silver recovered from 63.88 to 69.96. GBPCAD holds above broken-resistance-now-support 1.8721, watching UK CPI May Thursday for the next catalyst. FOMC today at 18:00 GMT is the dominant event for the entire 7-instrument basket.",
