      "analysis": "Price action: US30 gapped up +1.62% Monday to 51,671 on pre-FOMC relief, then extended to new all-time high 52,190 on Tuesday (+0.64% session) while NAS100 reversed. Value/industrial composition (Dow) is less multiple-sensitive than NAS100; sector rotation into defensive industrials/financials pre-FOMC. 51,671 support intact. Fundamentals: FOMC hold consensus. NFP +172K, unemployment 4.3%, Q1 earnings solid. Outlook: 3-day NEUTRAL. Too binary to position directionally. Hawkish hold = pullback to 51,671 floor (buy that dip). Neutral hold = extend above 52,190. Key read post-FOMC: close below 51,671 = distribution; close above = ATH continuation."
